---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import {
  compilerStages,
  evidenceRows,
  metrics,
  repositoryUrl,
  roadmap,
} from "../data/site";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<SiteLayout active="Overview">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <div class="hero-kicker">
        <span class="release-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>ABI8 Prefix + Full relocation · scoped sealed H20 records · performance pending</span>
      </div>
      <h1>Attention semantics.<br /><span>Compiled into state.</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">
        OrbitKV is an attention-lifecycle compiler plus a transactional,
        engine-neutral KV block runtime. It derives when model state can die,
        synthesizes its physical address plan, and authorizes reuse only after
        semantic and GPU execution frontiers agree. SGLang is the first
        adapter, not a full engine replacement.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}/docs/`}>Read the architecture</a>
        <a class="button quiet" href={`${base}/evidence/`}>Inspect evidence boundaries</a>
        <a class="button quiet" href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/capability-matrix.md`}>Capability matrix ↗</a>
      </div>
      <ul class="hero-facts" aria-label="Project boundaries">
        <li>Compiler-generated block plans</li>
        <li>Proof-carrying reclamation</li>
        <li>Explicit L1–L5 qualification</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="kernel-console" aria-label="OrbitKV layout program">
      <div class="console-bar">
        <span>orbitkv://layout/full-swa</span>
        <span class="console-state"><i></i> verified</span>
      </div>
      <div class="console-grid" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="console-body">
        <div class="console-ident">
          <span>RETENTION</span>
          <strong>TOKEN + FIXED STATE · ABI8</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-switch" aria-label="Physical lowering">
          <span class="selected">PAGED</span>
          <span>CUDA VMM</span>
        </div>
        <div class="console-flow">
          <div><small>analyze</small><strong>last_read(q, k)</strong><em>01</em></div>
          <div><small>prepare</small><strong>tail + copy + writes</strong><em>02</em></div>
          <div><small>publish</small><strong>immutable snapshot</strong><em>03</em></div>
          <div class="flow-active"><small>reclaim</small><strong>refs + done + ack</strong><em>04</em></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="console-footer">
        <span>fingerprint / sha256</span>
        <span>frontier / bitemporal</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="scope-strip" aria-label="Project boundary">
    <div><span>ORBITKV OWNS</span><strong>state semantics · logical blocks · generations · reclamation proof</strong></div>
    <div><span>ENGINE OWNS</span><strong>model execution · scheduling · attention kernels · request protocol</strong></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="compiler">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Compilation pipeline</p><h2>A block manager emitted from semantics.</h2></div>
      <p>
        Ring, append-only log, pinned region, and VMM are lowering choices.
        The checked lifetime program remains the source of truth.
      </p>
    </header>
    <ol class="execution-chain">
      {compilerStages.slice(0, 4).map((stage) => (
        <li>
          <span class="chain-key">{stage.key}</span>
          <div><h3>{stage.name}</h3><p>{stage.detail}</p></div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="section performance-section" id="evidence">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Qualification boundary</p><h2>Two sealed ABI8 records, two non-transferable scopes.</h2></div>
      <p>
        Exact source 6f62a23 passed all 12 stock/manager pairs across three
        epochs on one H20: Qwen2.5-7B Full and GPT-OSS-20B Full+SWA at B1/B4,
        using the official SGLang v0.5.17 base with the record-bound
        manager-side canonical loader patch, page16 BF16 NHD eager FA3. Outputs
        and request traces match exactly, seeded Prefix hits are observed, all
        arenas drain, and every Hybrid pair advances the required SWA counters.
        Relocation, MLA, fixed-state, overlap, Graph, speculation, distributed
        execution, and performance qualification are excluded from that Prefix
        seal.
        The exact request-private GDN+convolution runtime is integrated through
        allocation, initial clear, completion event, wait, retire, clear, and
        exact ACK. Qwen3.5 has scoped pair verification and Qwen3.8-27B-FP8 has
        a diagnostic run; both remain below L4 and neither demonstrates a
        throughput or memory benefit.
        Separately, the Rust core and Python runtime have host-tested two
        relocation cycles for one request-private Full class under full
        evacuation, and the SGLang periodic trigger is host-tested across two
        reclamation boundaries. Generation-safe packed fork and shared-tail
        COW are host-tested through Rust, raw ABI8, and Python FFI, including a
        repeated COW generation. Packed Prefix remains unsupported; packed COW
        has no H20/model qualification and is outside the relocation seal.
        Multi-request ABI8 relocation is also host-tested: one mark, prepare,
        submit, and complete call covers the scheduler batch; copies and the
        completion event are flattened, followed by one aggregate registry
        commit and one aggregate head replacement. Every mirror plan is built
        before writes, but mirror writes are not rollback-atomic; reclamation
        then uses one aggregate ACK. This is a post-mark fail-stop boundary, not rollback. The
        producer-to-copy event orders relocation, but completion is currently
        synchronized eagerly on the host, so there is no asynchronous overlap.
        The engine-neutral H20 component suite passes all seven cases at
        B1/B4/B32, including two cycles with real append, copy, and consumer
        streams, 257-byte payloads, ACK-gated generation reuse, and final drain.
        Separately, exact clean source <code>7e029310</code> is preflight-bound
        and sealed for scoped Qwen2.5-0.5B request-private Full relocation
        correctness and lifecycle. All 16 records / 8 Naive/Relocate B1/B4
        pairs across four balanced epochs are token-exact, fully drained, and
        failure-free; the bundled H20 component suite is 7/7. The manifest has
        <code>qualified=true</code>, but also
        <code>hardware_attested=false</code> and
        <code>performance_go=false</code>. B1 throughput/mean/median/p95 deltas
        are -1.3467%/+1.3651%/+2.0033%/+0.5141%; B4 deltas are
        +2.8096%/-2.7328%/+0.9810%/-19.8635%. These mixed observations establish
        no general speedup, capacity, memory, production, or full-replacement
        claim. The earlier dirty relocation diagnostic is historical and
        superseded.
        Request-private pressure telemetry is host-tested, but no real
        asynchronous GPU pressure run exists; fixed-state bytes and shared
        Prefix/fork retention amplification are excluded. Separate
        <code>orbitkv-runtime</code> and <code>orbitkv-reference</code> wheels
        exist, but the reference is not a complete engine and SGLang has not
        migrated to the SPI.
        The frozen ABI5-v5 H20 record remains historical only.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="metric-grid">
      {metrics.map((item) => (
        <article><strong>{item.value}</strong><div><h3>{item.label}</h3><p>{item.detail}</p></div></article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="evidence-table" role="table" aria-label="OrbitKV evidence summary">
      <div class="evidence-row evidence-head" role="row">
        <span role="columnheader">Result</span>
        <span role="columnheader">Value</span>
        <span role="columnheader">Contract</span>
        <span role="columnheader">Boundary</span>
      </div>
      {evidenceRows.slice(0, 4).map((item) => (
        <div class="evidence-row" role="row">
          <strong role="cell">{item.result}</strong>
          <code role="cell">{item.value}</code>
          <span role="cell">{item.contract}</span>
          <small role="cell">{item.boundary}</small>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <a class="text-link" href={`${base}/evidence/`}>Inspect methods and exclusions <span>→</span></a>
  </section>

  <section class="section roadmap-section" id="roadmap">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Next gates</p><h2>Expand the qualified ownership surface.</h2></div>
      <p>
        Snapshot, Prefix, fork, joint COW, page-owned reclamation, and the
        official SGLang cache seam now have a sealed, scoped Full/Full+SWA H20
        Prefix record. A second sealed clean-source record qualifies only
        request-private Full relocation correctness and lifecycle. The integrated exact
        request-private GDN+convolution lifecycle has
        model-specific H20 pair diagnostics, while the replacement production
        trigger, other families, clean L4 qualification, and performance remain
        pending. Repeated private Full relocation, multi-request batch
        relocation, and the SGLang periodic trigger are host-tested, but the
        batch event is still eager and host-blocking. Independent relocation
        hardware attestation and performance qualification, real asynchronous
        pressure/overlap, packed Prefix, packed shared-tail COW H20/model
        qualification, MLA, Graph, speculation, and distribution remain open
        gates.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="milestone-list">
      {roadmap.map((item) => (
        <article><span>{item.state}</span><div><h3>{item.name}</h3><p>{item.detail}</p></div></article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="closing-band">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Open source</p><h2>Compile lifetimes. Reuse with proof.</h2></div>
    <div class="closing-actions">
      <a class="button primary" href={`${base}/docs/`}>Architecture</a>
      <a class="button quiet" href={repositoryUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
